      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-146301",
      ":question/problem": "Suppose we have a random sample of size $n = 20$ from a population where $55%$ of the population has a particular characteristic. Let the random variable $X_{i}$ be equal to\n\n$X_{i} = {1, ith member of the sample has the characteristic; 0, otherwise$\n\nwhere $i = 1, \u2026, 20$. Find an approximate sampling distribution of the statistic $X = \u2211_(i = 1)^(20)X_{i}$.\n\n*Hint: You may assume that the population size is significantly larger than the sample size.*\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
